{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_3yjsx5t6nvaz3n64cgcdqhswrsbyrxvm3rxyuc2nx2dkpjirquaq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The translation is complete and verified.\n\n## Scope\n\n`c_src/` is a single-file library (`src/lib.c`, 157 lines) built by CMake into one shared object. `nm -D` on the C `.so` exports exactly **5** public symbols — no namespace/renaming macros in the header (`include/lib.h` declares only `overunder`; the other four are non-static and therefore exported too).\n\n## Result\n\n**`translation/Cargo.toml`** — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`, edition 2024, zero dependencies.\n**`translation/src/lib.rs`** — all 5 functions as `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern \"C\"`.\n\nSymbol diff (`comm -23 c_syms rust_syms`) is **empty**:\n\n| C export | Rust |\n|---|---|\n| `safe_double_to_int` | ✅ |\n| `process_with_fallthrough` | ✅ |\n| `copy_data_block` | ✅ |\n| `handle_pointer_operations` | ✅ |\n| `overunder` | ✅ |\n\n## Fidelity details that mattered\n\n- **Output goes through C `printf`**, declared via `unsafe extern \"C\"`, not `println!`. This gives identical `%.2f`/`%d` formatting *and* shares `stdout`'s buffer, so interleaving with a C caller's own prints matches. Verified: driver prints between calls appear in the same order.\n- **Signed overflow is reproduced, not fixed.** `d*d + a*a` overflows for large inputs; I used `wrapping_mul`/`wrapping_add` so e.g. `a=b=c=d=INT_MAX` yields `sqrt(2.0) → conv4 = 1`, and `a=INT_MIN, d=46341` wraps negative → `sqrt(neg) = NaN → 0`, both matching C. Same for `switch` accumulations, `value*2`, `a+b`, and the `total` sums.\n- **The `switch` fall-through is preserved** (case 5 accumulates all five additions, 0 resets to 0, default is -1) — kept as sequential wrapping adds mirroring the source.\n- **`copy_data_block`** does a raw 40-byte `copy_nonoverlapping` matching `memcpy(sizeof(DataBlock))`, so the 4+4 padding bytes copy too (confirmed by 500/500 full-struct `memcmp == 0`).\n- **`strncpy` semantics** (copy 6 bytes, zero-pad to n=19) implemented faithfully rather than as a plain string copy.\n- `safe_double_to_int` keeps the exact check order, including the dead-ish `isnan` branch placed *after* the range comparisons.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo build --release` — clean, no warnings.\n- Same C driver linked against each `.so`: **byte-for-byte equal** (2858 bytes).\n- Randomized differential harness, ~7000 calls across all 5 functions (INT_MIN/INT_MAX edges, random bit-pattern doubles incl. NaN/±inf/subnormals, values straddling the INT_MAX/INT_MIN conversion boundary, 500 struct copies): **315,050 bytes byte-for-byte equal**.\n- `ldd`/`nm -D --undefined-only`: only libc/libgcc; `sqrt` compiled to `sqrtsd`, no libm needed.\n\nTwo notes: `c_src/` is unmodified (md5sums unchanged, nothing written there). I also left behind a hidden scratch dir `.cbuild/` in the working root containing the C reference build and test harnesses — I tried to delete it but `rm -rf` was blocked by the sandbox permission prompt, so you may want to remove it yourself."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1589,"cache_read_input_tokens":41733,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1589,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"942b051c-091a-4893-99c4-a7e25935bca1","uuid":"4fb65c54-5f3e-4297-899c-3c3fc16b1dd1","timestamp":"2026-08-28T05:02:48.616Z"}
